			<view isee:template_view="template:2" isee:name="Terminology Guide 1" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<text_box z_index="-2" background="white" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="white" font_size="18pt" appearance="transparent" x="283" y="0" width="500" height="50" isee:locked="true">Navigation &amp; Terminology Guide</text_box>
				<button z_index="13" transparent="true" corner_radius="12" label="" isee:tooltip="" x="12.4665" y="566.546" width="26.1554" height="24.9464">
					<actions>
						<action target="previous_page">navigate</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<button z_index="15" transparent="true" corner_radius="12" label="" isee:tooltip="" x="1032.59" y="566.058" width="18.838" height="25.9222">
					<actions>
						<action target="next_page">navigate</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<isee:shape background="white" border_width="0.5" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" corner_radius="15" x="20" y="94" width="1026" height="456" isee:locked="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="90" y="180" width="540" height="301">Endogenous Model Behavior refers to how a system&apos;s behavior over time arises from its internal structure—such as feedback loops, delays, and accumulations—rather than from external inputs or random events. In other words, the model explains its own behavior through the interactions of its components.


In system dynamics, focusing on endogenous behavior helps users understand why things happen by revealing the causal mechanisms within the system, not just describing outcomes.


Example: If emissions rise in the model, it&apos;s not because we told the model to increase them—it&apos;s because internal variables (like population or energy demand) interacted in a way that led to that outcome.</text_box>
				<isee:shape z_index="15" border_color="#989898" border_width="0.5" opacity="1" transparent_background="false" x="683.15" y="95" width="14" height="454" kind="vline"/>
				<text_box text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="20pt" appearance="transparent" x="20" y="101.5" width="668" height="58">Endogenous Model Behavior (EMB)</text_box>
				<graphics_frame fill="none" x="776" y="230.5" width="200" height="200">
					<image width="512" height="512" size_to_parent="true" isee:transparency="0" isee:fixed_aspect_ratio="true">r../Graphics/feedback (1).png</image>
				</graphics_frame>
				<button z_index="47" background="#FBF5F0" font_weight="bold" font_size="8pt" border_color="#F5FFE0" transparent="false" corner_radius="15" isee:flat="false" isee:highlight_on_hover="true" isee:highlight_color="#D3F0FF" label="Return to Dashboard" isee:tooltip="" x="473" y="565" width="120" height="30" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Return_to_Dashboard_Button_from_Navigation_for_Guide">
