					<isee:navigation_item label="Gross Domestic Product" target="interface:6"/>
					<isee:navigation_item label="Uncertainty Ensemble and Representative Runs" target="interface:7"/>
				</isee:navigation_widget>
				<isee:shape z_index="48" background="#2D4A74" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="2.81818" y="561.019" width="39.0909" height="36" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Return_to_Dashboard_Button_from_Navigation_for_Guide" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<isee:shape z_index="49" background="#2D4A74" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="1022.46" y="561.019" width="39.0909" height="36" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Return_to_Dashboard_Button_from_Navigation_for_Guide" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<button z_index="47" background="#FBF5F0" font_weight="bold" font_size="8pt" border_color="#F5FFE0" transparent="false" corner_radius="15" isee:flat="false" isee:highlight_on_hover="true" isee:highlight_color="#D3F0FF" label="Return to Dashboard" isee:tooltip="" x="473" y="565" width="120" height="30" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Return_to_Dashboard_Button_from_Navigation_for_Guide">
					<actions>
						<action target="interface:27">navigate</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:2" isee:name="Terminology Guide 5" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<text_box z_index="-3" background="white" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="white" font_size="18pt" appearance="transparent" x="283" y="0" width="500" height="50" isee:locked="true">Navigation &amp; Terminology Guide</text_box>
				<button z_index="13" transparent="true" corner_radius="12" label="" isee:tooltip="" x="9.9323" y="566.546" width="25" height="25">
					<actions>
						<action target="previous_page">navigate</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<isee:shape background="white" border_color="#989898" border_width="0.5" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" corner_radius="15" x="20" y="94" width="1026" height="456" isee:locked="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box vertical_text_align="center" font_size="14pt" appearance="transparent" x="40.51" y="200" width="303.64" height="244.087">In FRIDA, uncertainty is explored by running the model many times under different assumptions. Each run represents one possible future based on uncertain inputs such as technology, behavior, and climate responses.

The full model generates 100,000 runs. Together, these runs form an uncertainty ensemble that captures a wide range of possible system behaviors, from low-impact to high-impact futures.</text_box>
				<isee:shape z_index="15" border_color="#989898" border_width="0.5" opacity="1" transparent_background="false" x="697.463" y="135.5" width="14" height="414" kind="vline"/>
				<text_box text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="20pt" appearance="transparent" x="20" y="98.3636" width="1026" height="35">Uncertainty Ensemble and Representative Runs</text_box>
				<isee:shape z_index="15" border_color="#989898" border_width="0.5" opacity="1" transparent_background="false" x="353.818" y="135.5" width="14" height="414" kind="vline"/>
				<text_box vertical_text_align="center" font_size="14pt" appearance="transparent" x="380.909" y="200" width="304.18" height="223.178">Displaying all 100,000 runs in an interactive tool is not practical. Instead, FRIDA uses 11 representative runs to provide a structured view of the uncertainty.

These runs are carefully selected to span the range of outcomes in the full ensemble. They are chosen to reflect different possible system trajectories, rather than being randomly sampled.</text_box>
				<text_box vertical_text_align="center" font_size="14pt" appearance="transparent" x="730.455" y="200" width="298.14" height="316.091">The full range of outcomes is ordered based on surface temperature anomaly. The distribution is then divided into 11 equal probability intervals. One run is selected from each interval to represent that portion of the uncertainty space.

The first run represents very low temperature outcomes, the last run represents very high outcomes, and the middle run represents the median trajectory.

Together, these runs provide a structured approximation of the uncertainty in the model, allowing users to explore how different futures may unfold.</text_box>
				<isee:shape border_color="#989898" border_width="0.5" x="21" y="125" width="1025" height="20" kind="hline"/>
				<text_box text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="20" y="166" width="342" height="38.82">Uncertainty Ensemble (Model Runs)</text_box>
				<text_box text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="362" y="166" width="342" height="38.82">Representative Runs Used in the ILE</text_box>
				<text_box text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="704" y="166" width="342" height="38.82">How the 11 Runs Are Chosen</text_box>
				<button z_index="15" font_size="14pt" transparent="true" corner_radius="12" label="" isee:tooltip="" x="1029.51" y="566.519" width="25" height="25">
					<actions>
						<action>start</action>
						<action isee:run_name_to_set="EMB">set_run_name</action>
						<action target="interface:8">navigate</action>
