				</isee:animation_object>
				<text_box background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_Intro_Appearance">The Model Behavior Page displays the evolution of three key variables from 1980 to 2150. 

The simulation begins when you press the play button  

The graph pauses at certain points to display crucial information.

The future trend after 2025 is projected based on the data from 1980 to 2025, which forms the trajectory for this projection.</text_box>
				<text_box background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_1980_Appearance">In 1980, the global economy expanded despite the 1979 oil crisis, leading to increased energy costs and inflation. 

Major economies like the U.S., Japan, and Western Europe led production, while developing nations like Asia and Latin America experienced growth through export-led policies. China had just begun market reforms. 

Scientists became increasingly aware of global warming, with research from NASA&apos;s GISS indicating rising CO₂ emissions from industrial activity and deforestation were driving long-term climate change. 

This had not become a major political issue.</text_box>
				<text_box background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_2000_Appearance">By 2000, the world experienced rapid economic growth due to globalization, technology, and emerging markets. 
The U.S. remained dominant, while China became a manufacturing hub. The European Union introduced the euro. 

However, global temperatures rose, leading to the Kyoto Protocol in 1997 to reduce emissions. Major economies 
like the U.S. refused to ratify it.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="-14" background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_2025_Appearance">In 2025, the world experiences moderate economic growth and record-breaking temperatures, highlighting the conflict between development and environmental sustainability. 

The World Bank predicted a 2.7% growth rate for 2025 and 2026, indicating a long-term low-growth trend. 

January 2025 became the hottest January on record, with surface air temperatures 1.75°C above pre-industrial levels (C3S), despite cooling La Niña conditions. These economic and climate signals a year of urgent global reckoning.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="-13" background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_2100_Appearance">By 2100, the global economy is expected to be carbon neutral, with many countries utilizing clean energy and advanced technologies like AI and biotechnology.

However, global GDP growth has slowed to around 2% annually due to sustainability prioritization. The legacy of past industrialization persists, with climate thresholds crossed and environmental instability persisting due to delayed green action. 

The 21st century presents a paradox of technological advancement and worsening climate impacts, redefining prosperity in terms of environmental health, social equity, and resilience for future generations.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="35" background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_2050_Appearance">
By 2050, the world is at a critical crossroads between economic growth and climate stability. 

Despite increased global GDP through technology and sustainable industries, surface temperatures have risen over 2°C, above pre-industrial levels, surpassing earlier warnings.  

Climate change is now a daily reality, displacing millions in vulnerable regions and intensifying extreme weather. Balancing prosperity with environmental survival is a significant challenge in this era.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="34" background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_2150_Appearance">By 2150, the world faces significant economic and environmental challenges, with GDP no longer a reliable indicator due to financial crises, resource shortages, and power shifts. Climate change intensifies, with surface temperatures rising to 3.6°C. 

Chaotic energy transitions, delayed infrastructure, and supply disruptions cause economic crashes, while food and water scarcity make basic needs unaffordable. Extreme weather conditions, including heatwaves and wildfires, reinforce global inequality and instability.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="-10" background="#082A5C" font_color="#F5FFE0" font_size="14pt" padding="20" x="2" y="95" width="320" height="450" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Goal_Setting_Message_Appearance">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#f5ffe0;&quot;&gt;Now that you&apos;ve seen the development of variables over time, define your goal by assigning target values for each variable and select the year you wish to achieve them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#f5ffe0;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#f5ffe0;&quot;&gt;Your decisions will shape the future - so pay attention to how your choices play out.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt;Use the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#00aa00;&quot;&gt;Next Page button &amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt;&quot;&gt; to proceed to the dashboard section of the ILE.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<numeric_input z_index="24" font_weight="bold" font_color="#082A5C" font_size="14pt" label_side="left" wrap_title="true" input_expands="true" x="982.182" y="110.909" width="65" height="20" isee:locked="true" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Goal_Setting_Message_Appearance" isee:tab_index="1" min="1" max="3" title="Target Value" isee:navigate_to="false" show_name="false">
