				<isee:annotation z_index="70" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="30.625" y="108.83" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="349.278" y="88" width="423.444" height="222.111">
						<text>A coal extraction technology tax is a fee (or subsidy) imposed on the equipment or processes used to mine coal, aimed at discouraging (or encouraging) fossil fuel production.

Supporters say it reflects coal’s environmental damage and encourages a shift to cleaner energy. It could also raise funds for climate or transition programs.

Critics argue it may hurt mining communities, raise energy prices, and weaken energy security in coal-dependent regions.

Debates center on fairness, regional impacts, and how quickly the coal industry should be phased down.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="71" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="372.969" y="108" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="6.278" y="106" width="346.444" height="223">
						<text>An oil extraction technology tax is a fee (or subsidy) imposed on the equipment or processes used to mine oil, aimed at discouraging (or encouraging) fossil fuel production.

Supporters say it reflects oil&apos;s environmental damage and encourages a shift to cleaner energy. It could also raise funds for climate or transition programs.

Critics argue it may hurt mining communities, raise energy prices, and weaken energy security in oil-dependent regions.

Debates center on fairness, regional impacts, and how quickly the oil industry should be phased down.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="73" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="716.699" y="108.83" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="308.278" y="102" width="367.444" height="223">
						<text>An gas extraction technology tax is a fee (or subsidy) imposed on the equipment or processes used to mine gas, aimed at discouraging (or encouraging) fossil fuel production.

Supporters say it reflects gas&apos;s environmental damage and encourages a shift to cleaner energy. It could also raise funds for climate or transition programs.

Critics argue it may hurt mining communities, raise energy prices, and weaken energy security in gas-dependent regions.

Debates center on fairness, regional impacts, and how quickly the gas industry should be phased down.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="90" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="31" y="315" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="350.278" y="275" width="393.444" height="237.5">
						<text>A coal energy production tax is a government fee on energy generated from coal plants, intended to reduce carbon emissions and pollution.

Supporters say it discourages coal use, promotes cleaner energy, and raises revenue for climate initiatives.

Critics warn it could increase power costs, harm coal-dependent jobs, and risk energy reliability.

Debate focuses on tax levels, transition timing, and support for affected communities.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="84" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="374" y="315" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="17.556" y="274.5" width="330.888" height="238.5">
						<text>A oil energy production tax is a government fee on energy generated from oil plants, intended to reduce carbon emissions and pollution.

Supporters say it discourages oil use, promotes cleaner energy, and raises revenue for climate initiatives.

Critics warn it could increase power costs, harm oil-dependent jobs, and risk energy reliability.

Debate focuses on tax levels, transition timing, and support for affected communities.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="86" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="717" y="315" width="20" height="20" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="307.278" y="289" width="367.444" height="223">
						<text>A gas energy production tax is a government fee on energy generated from gas plants, intended to reduce carbon emissions and pollution.

Supporters say it discourages gas use, promotes cleaner energy, and raises revenue for climate initiatives.

Critics warn it could increase power costs, harm gas-dependent jobs, and risk energy reliability.

Debate focuses on tax levels, transition timing, and support for affected communities.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
