				<switch z_index="102" font_size="11pt" label_side="left" isee:appearance="checkbox" x="119.49" y="145" width="140.02" height="30" isee:locked="true" title="Customize Forestation" show_name="true">
					<entity name="Government_Regulations.switch_forestation_policy"/>
					<reset_to after="never">0</reset_to>
				</switch>
				<isee:annotation z_index="93" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="32.3478" y="111.413" width="21.3043" height="17.1739" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="349.278" y="88" width="423.444" height="222.111">
						<text>A forestation policy is a government or organizational strategy aimed at managing, protecting, and expanding forested areas through activities like planting trees (afforestation) and preventing deforestation. 

Supporters argue that such policies combat climate change, preserve biodiversity, and support local economies. 

Critics, however, contend that poorly planned forestation can harm native ecosystems, displace communities, or prioritize commercial interests over environmental health. 

Current debates focus on balancing ecological restoration with social justice, ensuring native species planting, and integrating forestation with broader climate goals.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="97" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="375.905" y="112.682" width="24.1897" height="16.6364" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="16.278" y="101" width="328.07" height="295.111">
						<text>An irrigation policy is a government or organizational strategy focused on managing and distributing water resources to agricultural lands to improve crop production and ensure water efficiency. With this policy you set what percentage of the globe&apos;s cropland is irrigated.

Supporters argue that such policies increase food security, boost agricultural productivity, and support rural livelihoods.

Critics, however, contend that poorly designed irrigation can lead to water wastage, soil degradation, and negatively impact local ecosystems or communities.

Current debates focus on promoting sustainable water use, balancing agricultural needs with environmental protection, and integrating irrigation practices with climate resilience efforts.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="96" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="717.044" y="108" width="23.913" height="26" isee:locked="true">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="352.965" y="102" width="328.07" height="172.111">
						<text>A non-agricultural water use policy is a government or organizational strategy focused on managing and distributing water resources for domestic and industrial uses. With this policy you set how much freshwater is used for these purposes yearly.

Current debates focus on balancing water allocation between urban growth and ecosystem preservation, improving water-use efficiency, and addressing the impacts of climate change on water availability.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
