				<text_box z_index="125" background="#D7E3F2" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" padding="6" border_color="white" border_width="thin" border_style="solid" corner_radius="10" x="35" y="330" width="480" height="161" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_Visibility">These settings are not available when customizing &quot;Environmental Consciousness&quot;.</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="117" background="#D7E3F2" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="16pt" padding="6" border_color="white" border_width="thin" border_style="solid" corner_radius="10" x="550" y="330" width="480" height="161" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Interface.Text_Visibility_1">These settings are not available when customizing &quot;Food Demand&quot; or &quot;Animal Products&quot;.</text_box>
				<isee:annotation z_index="99" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="30" y="104" width="18" height="18">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="54.5025" y="99.6495" width="344.021" height="195.701">
						<text>Changes in per person food demand can significantly impact both the climate and the economy. Higher food demand per person especially for animal products increases greenhouse gas emissions, land use, and water consumption, contributing to climate change. Economically, it can raise food prices, strain agricultural systems, and shift market demand toward high-emission food sectors. Conversely, reducing per person demand or shifting toward plant-based diets can lower emissions, reduce environmental pressure, and potentially stabilize food markets, though it may disrupt certain agricultural industries.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="104" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="28.1739" y="305.876" width="21.6522" height="20.2472">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="118.54" y="158.727" width="344.021" height="149.351">
						<text>Changes in demand for animal products have notable effects on the climate. Increased consumption of meat, dairy, and other animal products raises greenhouse gas emissions, especially methane from livestock and contributes to deforestation, water use, and biodiversity loss. Reducing animal product demand, can lower emissions and environmental pressure, while shifting markets toward plant-based alternatives potentially disrupting traditional agricultural economies.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="105" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="544.488" y="103.706" width="19.0234" height="18.587">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="188.242" y="102.825" width="344.021" height="189.351">
						<text>Changes in per person energy demand directly influence both climate outcomes and economic activity. Higher energy demand per person typically leads to increased fossil fuel consumption, resulting in greater greenhouse gas emissions and climate change acceleration unless met by clean energy sources. Economically, rising energy demand can drive growth in energy sectors but also increase energy prices and infrastructure costs. Reducing per person energy demand through efficiency or conservation can cut emissions, and ease pressure on energy systems, though it may challenge industries reliant on high energy consumption.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<isee:annotation z_index="109" transparent="true" launcher_label="" show_by_default="false" hide_launcher="false" launch_on_hover="true" x="543.696" y="304.098" width="21.3043" height="23.8043">
					<popup hide_when_editing="true" x="630.788" y="168.324" width="344.021" height="135.176">
						<text>Changes in environmental consciousness, people’s awareness and concern for environmental issues can significantly affect their demand behaviors for food and animal products. Greater environmental consciousness often leads to more sustainable behaviors, such as reduced waste of food, and decreasing the fraction of animal products in their diets which collectively help lower greenhouse gas emissions and environmental degradation.</text>
					</popup>
				</isee:annotation>
				<button z_index="113" transparent="true" label="" isee:tooltip="See how behavior, food systems, and forests interact with climate" x="570" y="397" width="18" height="18" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Behavioral_Choices.switch_environmental_consciousness_policy">
					<actions>
						<action isee:reset_after="never" isee:reset_value="0" isee:controller_value="1" isee:entity='Interface."Causal_Link_-_Return_to_Dashboard_Button"'>control_entity</action>
						<action target="interface:95">navigate</action>
					</actions>
					<image width="256" height="256" size_to_parent="true">r../Graphics/loop Icon Black.png</image>
				</button>
				<button z_index="126" transparent="true" label="" isee:tooltip="See how behavior, food systems, and forests interact with climate" x="50" y="197" width="18" height="18" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity="Behavioral_Choices.switch_food_demand_policy">
