					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="271.616">Subsidies for solar, wind, and nuclear energy reduce the cost of clean technologies. This accelerates the shift away from fossil fuel use, increasing the speed of the energy transition. A faster transition reduces emissions and slows future temperature rise. These subsidies act on the same structural leverage point as a carbon tax, pushing the energy system toward cleaner technologies.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:5" isee:name="CLD 1 - Policy Effect 4" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
