						<entity name='"Solar-Wind-Nuclear_Subsidies"'/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_1.23"/>
						<entity name="Employment"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_1.8"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_1.44"/>
						<entity name="Investment"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="375.96">When the energy system shifts rapidly toward renewables, fossil-intensive industries can lose value quickly. Power plants, coal mines, and related infrastructure may become unprofitable, go bankrupt and become stranded assets. Rising bankruptcies put pressure on the financial system, reducing lending and therefore investment.  To restart lending and investment, governments may bailout the banks to try to stabilize the system. These bailouts support continued investment, but they also reflect underlying economic stress that can ripple through employment and overall growth.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:5" isee:name="CLD 1 - Policy Effect 5" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
