				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="149.046" y="119.091" width="325" height="275">When more people are employed, they pay income taxes and spend more, which boosts business activity and government revenue. When employment declines, tax collections fall and public budgets weaken. Economic growth has the same effect: a stronger economy raises revenue, while slow growth reduces it. These pressures shape how well governments can respond to economic or climate challenges.</text_box>
			</view>
