			<view isee:template_view="template:3" isee:name="CLD 2- Intro" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:shape z_index="16" background="#2D4A74" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="3.3913" y="561.821" width="74.7826" height="35" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_color="#2A6FB8" font_size="48pt" appearance="transparent" x="138" y="94.9091" width="790" height="59">S E E    T H E    S Y S T E M</text_box>
				<text_box font_style="italic" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="#2E3A46" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="183.909" y="162.909" width="698.182" height="101.818">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Beneath policies and headlines lies a connected feedback structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Diet, agriculture, land, and climate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt; continuously influence one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;You are about to explore how the full system unfolds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box font_style="italic" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="#2E3A46" font_size="6pt" appearance="transparent" x="183.909" y="374.091" width="698.182" height="160">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Hover over arrows to explore causal relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Hover over loop labels to understand each feedback cycle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Each page adds another loop. The system builds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;The first loop of this pathway appears next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_color="#2A6FB8" font_size="28pt" appearance="transparent" x="285.273" y="327.455" width="495.454" height="48.9091">HOW   TO   EXPLORE</text_box>
				<isee:shape border_color="#2A6FB8" border_width="0.4" opacity="0.49" x="335.091" y="279.091" width="395.818" height="24.5455" kind="hline"/>
				<text_box z_index="-6" background="white" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="white" font_size="18pt" appearance="transparent" x="283" y="0" width="500" height="50" isee:locked="true">Environmental Awareness, Diet Shift &amp; Forestation Dynamics</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:6" isee:name="CLD 2 - Loop 1" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.112"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.131"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.132"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="298.224">When animal product demand increases, livestock production expands and methane emissions rise. Higher methane emissions increase surface temperature anomaly, which raises perceived climate risk. Increased climate concerns strengthen dietary shifts toward plant-based foods, reducing animal product demand and lowering livestock production. This loop balances livestock activity through methane-driven climate feedback.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:6" isee:name="CLD 2 - Loop 3" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.110"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.131"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.112"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.132"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.122"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.122"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="293.636">When forest carbon uptake increases, more CO₂ is removed from the atmosphere, reducing surface temperature anomaly. Lower temperatures decrease perceived climate risk and weaken dietary shifts toward plant-based foods, increasing demand for animal products, which raises land pressure and reduces forest area. This reduction in forest area lowers carbon uptake, stabilizing the system through a balancing feedback between climate, diet, and forests.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:6" isee:name="CLD 2 - Loop 2" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.111"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.110"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.131"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.112"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.132"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.122"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.126"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.126"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="298.224">When demand for animal products rises, livestock production expands and more land is used for food and feed production. This reduces forest area and lowers carbon uptake, allowing more CO₂ to remain in the atmosphere and increasing surface temperature anomaly. Higher temperatures raise perceived climate risk, strengthening dietary shifts toward plant-based foods, which reduce animal product demand and contract livestock production. This creates a balancing feedback driven by climate impacts.
</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:6" isee:name="CLD 2 - Loop 4" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.119"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<entity name="Synthetic_Fertilizer_Production"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.128"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.109"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.112"/>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.127"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.110"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.131"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.111"/>
						<entity name="N₂O_Emissions"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.126"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.132"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.122"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="N₂O_Emissions"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.128"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.127"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<entity name="Synthetic_Fertilizer_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.119"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="309.318">When surface temperature anomaly increases, perceived climate risk rises and people shift toward plant-based diets. This reduces animal product demand and lowers livestock production. As livestock declines, less manure is available, increasing reliance on synthetic fertilizer production. Higher fertilizer use raises N₂O emissions, further increasing surface temperature anomaly. This creates a reinforcing feedback where climate-driven dietary change amplifies warming through agricultural nutrient dynamics.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 1" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Environmental_Consciousness"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.124"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="315.488">When environmental consciousness rises, people become more aware of the environmental impacts of their consumption choices. Food is one of the most visible and easily controlled areas of individual impact. As awareness increases, individuals shift more quickly toward toward plant-based diets.

This change begins at the demand level. It reflects shifting values and concern about climate risk rather than changes in production technology.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 2" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.117"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="243.636">As diets become more plant-based, demand for animal products declines. This shift reflects changing consumer preferences toward foods with lower environmental impact. As demand falls, producers adjust livestock production to avoid excess supply and economic losses. Over time, this leads to a contraction in livestock systems, aligning production levels with the new demand patterns.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 3" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.129"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.118"/>
						<entity name="CH₄_Emissions"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="285.117">Livestock production is a significant source of methane emissions, particularly from ruminant digestion and manure management. Methane is a powerful greenhouse gas with strong warming effects.

When livestock production increases, methane emissions rise. When livestock production declines, methane emissions fall. This creates a direct link between food demand and surface temperature anomaly.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 4" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.127"/>
						<entity name="Synthetic_Fertilizer_Production"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.119"/>
						<entity name="N₂O_Emissions"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.128"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="400">Modern crop production relies on synthetic fertilizers to maintain yields. Their production and application introduce reactive nitrogen into soils, where microbial processes generate nitrous oxide, a potent greenhouse gas.

Changes in livestock production alter nutrient availability through manure. When livestock production increases, more manure reduces reliance on synthetic fertilizers. When livestock production declines, less manure increases dependence on synthetic fertilizers and N₂O emissions. Agriculture therefore affects surface temperature not only through methane, but also through nitrogen-related emissions.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 5" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Land_Used_for_Food_and_Feed_Production"/>
						<entity name="Livestock_Production"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.126"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.123"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">Livestock production requires both grazing land and cropland for feed. When livestock production declines, less land is needed for food production. This reduces pressure to convert forests into agricultural land.

As agricultural land demand falls, forests regrow with a long delay. Changes in food demand therefore reshape land allocation.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 6" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<entity name="Forestation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.125"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="362.727">When forestation policy is implemented, forest area increases through restoration and planting initiatives. Unlike dietary change, which reduces land pressure indirectly, forestation acts immediately on land cover.

An increase in forest area strengthens carbon uptake from the atmosphere. This removes more CO₂ from the atmosphere and slows the rise in surface temperature anomaly. Forestation therefore influences the climate system from the land side, without first requiring changes in consumption behavior.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 7" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Forest_Area"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.113"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.114"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<entity name="Carbon_Uptake_by_Forests"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">Forests absorb carbon dioxide through photosynthesis and store carbon in biomass and soils. When forest area increases, either through reduced land pressure or forestation policy, total carbon uptake rises.

Higher carbon uptake removes more CO₂ from the atmosphere. This weakens radiative forcing and slows temperature increase. Forest dynamics therefore directly shape long-term climate outcomes.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:7" isee:name="CLD 2 - Policy Effect 8" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.120"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.116"/>
						<entity name="Animal_Product_Demand"/>
						<entity name="Surface_Temperature_Anomaly"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_2.121"/>
						<entity name="Perceived_Climate_Change_Risk"/>
						<entity name="Diet_Shift_towards_Plant_Based_Foods"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="336.363">As surface temperature anomaly rises, climate-related impacts become more visible and tangible. This increases perceived climate change risk. Higher perceived risk strengthens dietary shifts toward plant-based foods.

Through this pathway, changes in the physical climate system influence consumption behavior. These behavioral shifts feed back into animal product demand, livestock production, land use, and emissions, linking human decisions directly to climate outcomes within a feedback structure.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:3" isee:name="CLD 2 - END" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="14pt" padding="10" appearance="transparent" x="35" y="105.218" width="425" height="345.84">The Complete System

You have now explored how environmental consciousness, dietary shifts, livestock production, land use, forest area, methane and nitrous oxide emissions, atmospheric CO₂, and surface temperature interact through reinforcing and balancing feedback loops.

Policies such as environmental awareness initiatives and forestation efforts influence key links in the system, shaping how the food–land–climate system evolves over time.

Here is the entire causal loop diagram. It brings together behavioral change, agricultural production, land dynamics, and climate feedback into one connected system, showing how human choices and Earth system processes are tightly intertwined.</text_box>
				<isee:shape z_index="30" background="#2C4973" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="1018.53" y="561.019" width="46.9565" height="36" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box z_index="22" font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_size="14pt" appearance="transparent" x="687.273" y="84.6364" width="167.273" height="17.9086">Causal Structure</text_box>
				<isee:navigation_widget z_index="19" border_width="thin" border_style="none" item_spacing="3" appearance="tabs" corner_radius="5" selected_item_background="#FAF4F0" item_background="#DDD9D5" orientation="horizontal" x="77.5" y="54.6" width="356.364" height="25">
					<isee:navigation_item label="Understanding the System" target="interface:96"/>
					<isee:navigation_item label="Understanding the Policy Effects" target="interface:100"/>
				</isee:navigation_widget>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_2"/>
					<isee:highlight_list/>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="white" font_size="18pt" appearance="transparent" x="0" y="0" width="1066" height="50">Environmental Awareness, Diet Shift &amp; Forestation Dynamics</text_box>
