			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:3" isee:name="CLD 3- Intro" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:shape z_index="16" background="#2D4A74" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="3.3913" y="561.821" width="74.7826" height="35" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_color="#2A6FB8" font_size="48pt" appearance="transparent" x="138" y="94.9091" width="790" height="59">S E E    T H E    S Y S T E M</text_box>
				<text_box font_style="italic" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="#2E3A46" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="10.2726" y="153.909" width="1045.45" height="137">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;Fast policy implementation forces rapid change.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;It can drive growth, but also creates inflation, failed investments, and stranded assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic;&quot;&gt;This pathway explains why speed creates trade-offs between growth and stability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box font_style="italic" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="#2E3A46" font_size="16pt" appearance="transparent" x="183.909" y="374.091" width="698.182" height="160">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Segoe UI&apos;; font-size:9pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Hover over arrows to explore causal relationships.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Hover over loop labels to understand each feedback cycle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Each page adds another loop. The system builds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:12pt; font-style:italic; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;The first loop of this pathway appears next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_color="#2A6FB8" font_size="28pt" appearance="transparent" x="285.273" y="327.455" width="495.454" height="48.9091">HOW   TO   EXPLORE</text_box>
				<isee:shape border_color="#2A6FB8" border_width="0.4" opacity="0.49" x="335.091" y="283.636" width="395.818" height="24.5455" kind="hline"/>
				<text_box z_index="-6" background="white" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_color="white" font_size="18pt" appearance="transparent" x="283" y="0" width="500" height="50" isee:locked="true">Speed of Policy Implementation &amp; Economic Feedback</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:8" isee:name="CLD 3 - Loop 1" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.8"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.3"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.2"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.19"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.20"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Investment"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.2"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Investment"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.3"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="298.224">When economic output increases, it supports further transformation of the energy system by enabling more resources to be allocated toward change. As energy production transformation accelerates, it drives higher levels of investment in new technologies and infrastructure. Increased energy investment further boosts economic output through increased economic activity. This creates a reinforcing feedback loop where transition and economic growth amplify each other.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:8" isee:name="CLD 3 - Loop 2" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.7"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.20"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.19"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.2"/>
						<entity name="Inflation"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.9"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.6"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.3"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.8"/>
						<entity name="Transition_Malinvestment"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.5"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Investment"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.6"/>
						<entity name="Inflation"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.7"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<entity name="Transition_Malinvestment"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.5"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="298.224">As economic output increases, it accelerates the transformation of the energy system. When this transformation happens rapidly, it increases the likelihood of inefficient or poorly coordinated investments. These malinvestments raise costs across the system, contributing to inflation. Higher inflation reduces economic output by increasing production costs and reducing efficiency. This creates a balancing feedback loop that limits growth when transition occurs too quickly.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:8" isee:name="CLD 3 - Loop 3" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" use_visible_list="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:visible_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.7"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.20"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.10"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.5"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Investment"/>
						<entity name="Stranded_Fossil_Energy_Assets"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.12"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.6"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.9"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.3"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<entity name="Inflation"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.19"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.2"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.8"/>
						<entity name="Transition_Malinvestment"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.11"/>
					</isee:visible_list>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<entity name="Stranded_Fossil_Energy_Assets"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.4"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.10"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.11"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="298.224">Higher economic output supports faster transformation of the energy system. As transformation accelerates, existing fossil energy infrastructure and investments can lose value before the end of their expected lifetime. These stranded assets create financial losses and reduce economic activity. The decline in economic output slows further transformation, creating a balancing feedback loop driven by disruptions in existing industries.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 1" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.1"/>
						<entity name="Speed_of_Implementation_Energy_Tax_or_Subsidy"/>
						<entity name="Big_Changes_in_Energy_Costs"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">When policies are implemented very quickly, they create large and sudden changes in energy costs. These rapid cost shifts force producers, investors, and consumers to respond immediately rather than gradually.

Instead of allowing the system to adapt over time, fast implementation compresses adjustment into a short period. This creates pressure across the energy system and triggers rapid structural change.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 2" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Big_Changes_in_Energy_Costs"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.13"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">Large changes in energy costs create strong incentives to shift how energy is produced and used. Firms respond by accelerating the transition toward new technologies and energy sources.

This rapid response drives transformation in the energy production system. However, when changes are too large or too sudden, the system must adjust under pressure rather than through coordinated planning.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 3" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Energy_Investment"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.2"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.3"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">As the energy system transforms, it requires significant investment in infrastructure, technology, and production capacity. These investments increase economic activity by creating demand for labor, materials, and capital.

Higher levels of investment contribute to increased economic output. This creates a positive link between transformation and growth, especially during periods of rapid transition.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 4" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.5"/>
						<entity name="Transition_Malinvestment"/>
						<entity name="Inflation"/>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.6"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">When transformation happens too quickly, investments are often made under time pressure with limited coordination. This increases the risk of inefficient or poorly targeted investments.

These malinvestments raise costs across the system and contribute to inflation. As inflation rises, production becomes more expensive and economic efficiency declines.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 5" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
						<entity name="Inflation"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.7"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">Inflation increases the cost of goods, services, and production inputs. As costs rise, firms face lower margins and reduced efficiency, while consumers experience reduced purchasing power.

These effects reduce overall economic output. As a result, the economy slows down even though transformation is still underway.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 6" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Energy_Production_Transformation"/>
						<entity name="Stranded_Fossil_Energy_Assets"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.10"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">As the energy system shifts rapidly, existing fossil energy infrastructure can lose value before the end of its expected lifetime. Power plants, extraction systems, and related investments may no longer be economically viable.

These stranded assets represent lost value in the system and reflect the difficulty of replacing existing infrastructure too quickly.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 7" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Stranded_Fossil_Energy_Assets"/>
						<item uid="CLD_Policy_3.11"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">When fossil energy assets lose value, firms experience financial losses and investment returns decline. This can lead to reduced economic activity, job losses, and financial instability.

These effects reduce economic output and slow down further transformation of the energy system.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:9" isee:name="CLD 3 - Policy Effect 8" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="110" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list>
						<entity name="Speed_of_Implementation_Energy_Tax_or_Subsidy"/>
						<entity name="Economic_Output"/>
					</isee:highlight_list>
				</isee:model_view>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="16pt" padding="20" appearance="transparent" x="150" y="120" width="325" height="291.818">Slower policy implementation allows the system to adapt over time. Investments can be planned more efficiently, existing industries can adjust gradually, and infrastructure can be replaced without sudden shocks.

This reduces the risks of inflation, malinvestment, and stranded assets. As a result, the transition becomes more stable while still achieving long term change.</text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:3" isee:name="CLD 3 - END" background="#082A5C" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="180" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<text_box z_index="16" font_size="14pt" padding="10" appearance="transparent" x="35" y="105.218" width="425" height="402.149">The Complete System

You have now explored how implementation speed, energy system transformation, investment, inflation, and stranded assets interact through reinforcing and balancing feedback loops.

Faster implementation accelerates change, but also creates pressure through inflation, inefficient investments, and financial disruption. Slower implementation allows the system to adjust more gradually, reducing these risks.

Here is the entire causal loop diagram. It brings together policy timing, economic dynamics, and system constraints into one connected system, showing how the speed of change shapes both progress and stability.</text_box>
				<isee:shape z_index="30" background="#2C4973" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent_background="false" x="1018.53" y="561.019" width="46.9565" height="36" block_mouse="true" kind="rectangle"/>
				<text_box z_index="22" font_weight="bold" text_align="center" font_size="14pt" appearance="transparent" x="687.273" y="84.6364" width="167.273" height="17.9086">Causal Structure</text_box>
				<isee:navigation_widget z_index="19" border_width="thin" border_style="none" item_spacing="3" appearance="tabs" corner_radius="5" selected_item_background="#FAF4F0" item_background="#DDD9D5" orientation="horizontal" x="77.5" y="54.6" width="350.909" height="25">
					<isee:navigation_item label="Understanding the System" target="interface:110"/>
					<isee:navigation_item label="Understanding the Policy Effects" target="interface:113"/>
				</isee:navigation_widget>
				<isee:model_view z_index="16" x="485" y="80" width="570" height="470" isee:locked="true" zoom="0.5" center_x="576" center_y="480" locked_view="true" show_animations="true" show_ltm_table="false" include_documentation="true">
					<model name="CLD_Policy_3"/>
					<isee:highlight_list/>
				</isee:model_view>
				<button z_index="16" background="#FBF5F0" font_weight="bold" font_color="#082A5C" font_size="8pt" border_color="#F5FFE0" border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent="false" corner_radius="15" isee:flat="false" isee:highlight_on_hover="true" isee:highlight_color="#D3F0FF" label="Return to Pathway Menu" isee:tooltip="" x="473" y="565" width="120" height="30" isee:conditional_immediately_update_on_user_input="true" isee:conditional_use_active_value="true" isee:conditional_entity='Interface."Regular_-_Causal_Structure_Skip_to_End_Button"'>
